    "blurb": "End-to-end local AI workflow",
    "overview": "Run a complete Camunda 8 workflow powered by a locally hosted AI model via Ollama — no cloud API costs, full data privacy, fully self-hosted.",
    "rating": null,
    "reviewCount": 0,
    "mobileBundleId": null,
    "mobileAppStoreId": null
  },
  "overview": {
    "splashTitle": "Run local AI prompts without cloud costs",
    "splashDescription": "This blueprint demonstrates a complete, working Camunda 8 Self-Managed process that calls a locally running AI model through Ollama — with no cloud AI dependency. It shows the full path from BPMN process design to a live AI response: a \"Give Prompt to Model\" user task, a \"Process the Prompt\" service task powered by the custom Ollama outbound connector, and a \"Result\" task returning the model's output. The blueprint includes the Docker Compose configuration needed to bridge a containerized Camunda Connectors runtime to an Ollama instance running on the host machine, along with the Camunda Modeler element template that makes the Ollama task available natively in the BPMN palette. It's intended as a starting reference for teams who want to run open-weight models (llama3.2, mistral, qwen2.5, gpt-oss:20b) inside their workflows without per-request cloud AI billing.",
    "imageUrl": "https://d3bql97l1ytoxn.cloudfront.net/app_resources/871406/overview/img16269040366677534986.png?dc647e93abea6562fd489581f4f67582",
